und in a run of big losses through the middle game. The lead was close to even until move 13, when Opus 5.5's F3 lost 12.1 points and the lead fell to -16.9. Opus 5.5 then pushed along the top and right edges (G7, H8, J8), each losing 15 points or more while White answered at the top. A lead of -20.6 at move 19 never recovered, and the game ended after White swept the lower left.", "moments": [{"turn": 9, "text": "Opus 5.5's G4 lost 4.0 points and took the lead from -0.3 to -4.3. The engine preferred F3. It was the first real slip in a game that had been level, and White's E7 answer lost 2.4 points, so the lead was still within reach."}, {"turn": 13, "text": "F3 lost 12.1 points, dropping Black's lead from -4.8 to -16.9, while the engine wanted B5. After it, White's E-file wall (E3 through E5) sat beside Black's stones at F3, F4 and D3. This was the move that turned a close game into a hard one."}, {"turn": 14, "text": "The 10k's G8 lost 14.6 points and the lead came back from -16.9 to -2.3. The engine's choice was E2. White was given a way back into a game that was nearly decided, and did not take the lower side."}, {"turn": 19, "text": "J8 was the worst move of the game for Opus 5.5, losing 17.9 points and taking the lead from -2.7 to -20.6. It was the third edge-side move in a row (G7, H8, J8) costing 15 points or more, each time with E2 as the engine's pick. The lower side stayed open the whole time."}, {"turn": 21, "text": "G2 lost 15.5 points and the lead went from -13.4 to -28.9, the engine preferring B6. White's F2 on the move before had already cut in below the Black stones. After this the lead stayed beyond -28 and the game was about the margin."}, {"turn": 18, "text": "The 10k's H9 lost 16.1 points, the worst of White's moves, though the lead only moved from -18.8 to -2.7 in Black's favour. Opus 5.5 gave the points straight back with J8 on the next turn, so White's error cost nothing in the end."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py and count.py only parse a pasted board and compute group liberties and an area count of the current position (count.py flood-fills empty regions, no look-ahead), and the other commands just cat notes and append to CLAUDE.md and games.md. Nothing ran that ranks candidate moves or plays continuations.", "stop": false}}